    "result_text": "The acceptance test is the only test suite, and all tests pass with a successful build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation:\n\n**New file** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`: a small helper (mirroring the existing `TelephoneE164` pattern) whose `normalize(String)` trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, then expands street-type abbreviations token-wise (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A `null`/blank input normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n**`ValidateOwnerFields.java`**: replaced the raw `checkRequired(\"address\", \u2026)` with a `normalizeAddress` step that normalizes the address and stores the canonical form back on the request. If the address is blank *after* normalization it adds an `\"address\"` error (\u2192 400); otherwise it republishes the normalized value.\n\n**Why nothing else needed changing:** the pipeline runs `validate \u2192 checkTelephone \u2192 checkHousehold \u2192 build \u2192 assignHousehold`. Because `ValidateOwnerFields` writes the normalized address back onto the request (which `@Val` hands to every later step by reference), every downstream consumer already operates on the normalized form:\n- `BuildOwner` maps the normalized request into the `Owner`, so it's stored and returned normalized.\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` (duplicate detection) and `AssignHousehold` (shared household id) compare `request`/`owner` addresses against stored owners \u2014 all now normalized, so comparisons use the normalized form consistently on both sides.\n\n**Results:** all three new acceptance tests pass \u2014 whitespace/case normalization (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`), abbreviation expansion (`\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`), and blank-after-normalization rejection (`\"   \"` \u2192 400) \u2014 and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
